0,Kugu Nganhcara language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kugu_Nganhcara_language,"January 1, 2026 - Kugu-Muminh (Wik-Muminh), also known as Kugu- or Wik-Nganhcara (Wikngenchera), is a Paman language spoken on the Cape York Peninsula of Queensland, Australia, by several of the Wik peoples.",Kugu-Muminh,Australian
1,Music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Australia,"Contemporary fusions of indigenous and Western styles are exemplified in the works of Yothu Yindi, No Fixed Address, Geoffrey Gurrumul Yunupingu and Christine Anu, and mark distinctly Australian contributions to world music.",Kugu-Muminh,Australian
